  "final_message": "CI is failing because `analytics-ingest` still requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). My earlier premise, that nothing reads the field, was wrong. I've put `channel` back, so the `OrderPlaced` event carries it again, as do the order model and `POST /orders` validation. `npm test` passes (39/39). I haven't run CI or `npm run arch`. I haven't confirmed that `analytics-ingest` now passes.\n\nThe working tree now differs from HEAD (commit `8bedb13`, \"gen\"), which I didn't create. That commit has the version without `channel`. Git will show the restore as uncommitted changes in nine files until you commit it.\n\nThe ARCH-4 contract check isn't in this repo, so I couldn't read the full contract. I restored `channel` in the event payload, the order model, request parsing and validation, the docs and the tests. I restored the model and request parsing too because the event is built from the order and needs the value.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first, and that change is in another repo. After that, the removal can go back in, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump.",
